This file has two parts: a short preamble from the licensor (below), then the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, reproduced unchanged. The licence text is the legal grant; the preamble only states scope and adds one permission. Nothing in the preamble takes away any right the licence text gives you.

1. Not open source. This software is source-available under the licence below, which permits noncommercial use. It is not open source software, and it is not licensed for commercial use, resale, or use to run a paid or hosted audit service. If you want to use it commercially, ask the licensor.

2. Scope: this repository only. This licence covers only the files in this repository. It grants no right to any EvaluatedApplications.* package or to any other software of the licensor. The CouncilAudit library (src/CouncilAudit) and its tests (src/CouncilAudit.Tests) need no EvaluatedApplications.* package and build and run under this licence alone. A command-line tool and a prototype that use EvaluatedApplications.HoloDb are NOT in this repository; those packages are under their own commercial licence, and anyone who runs software that depends on them needs their own right to the package under its terms.

3. Additional permission for journalism and verification. In addition to the licence below, you may read, build, run and check this software against the council data published with it, in order to verify, criticise or correct its results or the licensor's published findings, and to publish that verification, criticism or correction, even if you are a commercial publisher or work for a commercial organisation. This permission does not allow resale, a hosted or paid audit service, or using the software to sell audits. It does not widen any other term of the licence below.

4. Data is separate. The council spending data and any tables derived from it are not part of this software and are not covered by this licence. They are under their own terms: the councils' own publications (typically the Open Government Licence) and the licensor's published derived tables.

5. No warranty. As the licence below says, the software is provided as is. A flagged row is an exception to be checked, not a finding of error or wrongdoing by anyone.

